    def resolve_names (self, *, names, max_close_matches = None):
        """Looks up words or phrases (for example from a user's question) among the names of the open
        project before they are passed to other commands: stories, layers, layer combinations, building
        materials, composites, profiles, surfaces, fills, lines, zone categories, element types (by API
        name and, from Archicad 27, by the name the Archicad interface shows), properties (by name, and
        by group and name together) and classifications (systems by name and version, items of every
        system by name and ID). For each name it returns 'found' with the items named exactly so,
        'closeMatches' with the nearest names, best first (ranked by differences in case, accents,
        spacing and separators, shared words, one name containing the other and a few differing
        characters), or 'notFound' when nothing in the project is close, meaning the project has no such
        item and it must not be guessed. Each match carries what the other commands take: the story
        index, the attribute id and index, the elementType, the propertyId (with the property's group,
        value type and the classification items a custom property is available for), or the
        classificationSystemId and classificationItemId. Matching is lexical and deterministic. Read
        only.

        Tapir command ResolveNames (Tapir 2.0.0): https://archicad-api.com/archicad-addon/#ResolveNames

        Arguments:
        names (array of object, required): The words or phrases to look up in the open project, for
            example taken from a user's question.
        max_close_matches (maxCloseMatches, integer, optional): The most close matches returned for one
            word, best first. The default is 5.
        """
        return self.run ('ResolveNames', _Parameters (('names', names), ('maxCloseMatches', max_close_matches)))

